# Caddy in front of Sunbird: TLS here, everything else to the server on
# 127.0.0.1:8080, which is not reachable from outside. Replace the host name
# with yours; Caddy obtains and renews the certificate, and redirects plain
# HTTP to HTTPS.
#
# TLS is not optional. The fragment of a link never reaches the server, but
# the JavaScript this serves is what reads it; over plain HTTP anyone on the
# path can replace that JavaScript. See README.md, Deployment.
#
# Caddy sets X-Forwarded-For to the address it was connected from, replacing
# whatever the client sent, and connects from 127.0.0.1, which is why the
# example config lists 127.0.0.1 in trusted_proxies. Request bodies are
# streamed through, not buffered, so the server's size, quota and disk checks
# see them as they arrive.

files.example.org {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080

	# Once a browser has seen this, it refuses plain HTTP for the host for a
	# year: a network in the path cannot downgrade a later visit.
	header Strict-Transport-Security "max-age=31536000"
}
